{"seq":1,"mint":"C7","verb":"claim","status":"ok","model":"openai/gpt-5.6-luna","approach":"split","literals":false,"findings":[{"kind":"contradicts","clause":"`ExtentEntry` already carries four `#[serde(default)]` fields whose absence is documented as \"not recorded\" rather than as a default value — `world_root`, `kind`, `out_len` and `matcher`","clause_quoted":true,"facts":[],"why":"The captured documentation explicitly says `kind`, `out_len`, and `matcher` use `None` to mean \"not recorded\", but `world_root` is a `String` whose missing value deserializes to the default empty string. Its documentation says an empty root has a specific meaning, not that absence means \"not recorded\". The same captured struct also contains a fifth `#[serde(default)]` field, `pattern`, so the asserted four-field description is not accurate.","quoted":false,"rejected_span":"    #[serde(default)]\n    pub world_root: String,\n    pub world_state: String,\n    /// What kind of observation this entry came from, or `None` for one\n    /// minted before the field existed.\n...\n    /// `None` means *not recorded*, never *some default kind*: a fact\n...\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub kind: Option<crate::pending::ObservationKind>,\n...\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub out_len: Option<usize>,\n...\n    #[serde(default)]\n    pub matcher: Option<crate::pending::Matcher>,"}],"at":1790112501,"cost":0.00634135,"elapsed_ms":15015,"attempts":2,"not_verbatim":0,"literals_refuted":0,"not_a_quantity":0,"kind_off_verb":0,"refuted":0}
